ation boundaries and trusted completion hooks, excluding raw deltas and interrupted partials from archive truth.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/team-impl-log.md:250:- Story 3 owns authenticated archive read route/client surface, durable reload/environment-loss reads, empty state, access checks, and per-entry degraded metadata.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/team-impl-log.md:251:- Story 4 owns deterministic turn derivation and cached rebuildable turn projections without mutating archive entries.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/team-impl-log.md:252:- Story 5 owns non-summarizing structural derived views over turns, list/refresh routes, provenance to turns/archive entries, degraded/conflict behavior, and client rendering.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:35:The platform also preserves a full-fidelity canonical archive of process\ndocs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:72:tools, artifacts, sources, archive, and review.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:79:| Processes | Fastify | Process lifecycle control, phase transitions, delegated work orchestration, process-module dispatch | Projects, Artifacts, Environments, Archive | Process types are executed through this domain and do not bypass it with ad hoc controllers |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:84:| Archive | Fastify + Convex + cache/index layers | Full-fidelity low-level process history, turn derivation, later chunk/view derivation inputs | Processes | Canonical history is preserved at entry grain; turns and chunks are derived over it |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:85:| Review Workspace | Client + Fastify-backed APIs | Markdown/Mermaid rendering, artifact reading, pinned-context review surface, package viewing | Artifacts, Processes, Archive | Review lives in the same platform surface as orchestration, and eligibility follows process reference or pinned package context rather than artifact ownership |\n