at process\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:126:- **TC-1.1b: Finalized model message archived**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:129:  - Then: A `model_message` archive entry is appended for that process\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:130:- **TC-1.1c: Process event archived**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:133:  - Then: A `process_event` archive entry is appended for that process\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:135:**AC-1.2:** The canonical archive supports the PRD entry taxonomy.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:137:- **TC-1.2a: Required archive entry kinds accepted**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:138:  - Given: The platform appends finalized archive entries\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:140:  - Then: The archive accepts `user_message`, `model_message`, `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, and `process_event`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:141:- **TC-1.2b: Unsupported archive entry kind rejected**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:142:  - Given: A caller attempts to append an unsupported archive entry kind\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:144:  - Then: The platform rejects the entry and does not append a partial archive record\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:146:**AC-1.3:** Archive entries preserve order within one process.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:148:- **TC-1.3a: Process archive entries read in stable order**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:149:  - Given: Multiple archive entries exist for one process\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:150:  - When: The archive is read in ascending order\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:153:  - Given: Multiple archive entries have the same timestamp\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:154:  - When: The archive is read\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:157:**AC-1.4:** Archive entries can link to related process, artifact, source, or tool context without requiring those related records to remain current.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:159:- **TC-1.4a: Archive entry links to artifact context**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:160:  - Given: An archive entry relates to an artifact version or artifact event\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:161:  - When: The archive entry is read\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:163:- **TC-1.4b: Archive entry survives missing related context**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:165:  - When: The archive entry is read\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:166:  - Then: The archive entry remains visible with bounded degraded related-context metadata\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:168:### 2. Keeping Streaming State Separate from Canonical Archive\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:170:The browser may receive live updates while work is active. The archive receives\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:171:only completed entries. The live current-object model and canonical archive do\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:177:4. The platform appends only completed objects to the archive\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:178:5. Interrupted partial objects remain outside canonical archive truth\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:182:**AC-