e entry shape\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive.md:173:- Raw streaming deltas and interrupted partial objects cannot append finalized archive entries\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive.md:174:- Retried completion events do not duplicate archive rows\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive.md:175:- Existing live process upserts continue to update current browser state without creating archive rows by themselves\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive.md:176:- Tests cover TC-2.1a through TC-2.3b plus live/archive separation and compatibility mapping from the test plan\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:1:# Technical Design: Epic 7 Archive and Derived Views\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:6:process archive, turn derivation, and non-summarizing structural derived views.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:8:history while keeping live process state, turns, and derived views separate from\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:13:| Reviewers | Validate that archive work follows the core platform architecture |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:19:- Epic: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:20:- Test plan: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:26:surfaces, but the archive domain is coherent enough for one index document.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:30:Epic 7 is implementation-ready. It is scoped to canonical finalized archive\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:31:entries, deterministic turn derivation, minimal structural derived views, and\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:38:| Current `processHistoryItems` vocabulary differs from canonical archive taxonomy | Baseline, Tech Design Question 2 | Design adds new `archiveEntries` while bridging current history for compatibility. No historical migration/backfill is included. | Resolved - clarified |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:39:| Finalization boundary must prevent raw deltas and interrupted partial objects | AC-2.x, Tech Design Question 3 | Design introduces `ArchiveFinalizationService` and `finalizationKey` idempotency. Only completed objects call append. | Resolved |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:40:| Turn and derived-view persistence could accidentally become canonical truth | AC-4.x, AC-5.x | Design treats turns and derived views as cached/rebuildable projections over `archiveEntries`. | Resolved |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:41:| Minimal derived view could drift into summarization | AC-5.x | Design limits derived views to structural `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` records without generated summary body. | Resolved |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:42:| Provenance links must not duplicate Epic 5/6 ownership logic | AC-6.x | Design stores nullable related ids and enriches through existing artifact/source services at read time. Archive entries remain visible when enrichment degrades. | Resolved |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:45:archive finalization policy, read orchestration, turn derivation, and derived\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:53:| 1 | What durable schema stores archive entries, sequence numbers, related references, and idempotency keys? | Add `archiveEntries` with `projectId`, `processId`, `entryKind`, `sequence`, `finalizationKey`, `sourceObjectId`, body fields, related ids, status, and timestamps. Convex assigns sequence inside an append mutation and enforces `finalizationKey` idempotency per process. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:54:| 2 | What compatibility mapping bridges `processHistoryItems` and live updates, and is migration/backfill in scope? | Add compatibility helpers that map new finalized archive entries to existing process-history surfaces where needed. Existing `processHistoryItems` remain the legacy presentation read model. No historical migration/backfill is in scope for Epic 7. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:55:| 3 | What finalization boundary determines when entries are archived? | `ArchiveFinalizationService` is called only from completion points: accepted user responses, completed model/runtime objects, completed script emissions, finalized tool calls/results, and process events. Raw live deltas and interrupted partial objects never call append. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:56:| 4 | What derivation rules group archive entries into turns? | Turn derivation is deterministic over ordered archive entries. A `user_message` starts a new turn; following model/reasoning/script/tool/process entries attach to the active turn until the next `user_message`. Tool call/result correlation keeps paired tool entries in the same turn. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:57:| 5 | Should turns be persisted, computed on read, or cached with rebuild? | Turns are cached derived records in `archiveTurns` for bounded reads, but they are rebuildable from `archiveEntries` and never canonical truth. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:58:| 6 | What minimal derived-view representation should Epic 7 implement? | Implement structural `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` views with source turn/archive ids, optional labels, and status metadata. No model-generated summaries or summarization prompts. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:59:| 7 | How should source/artifact provenance link without duplicating ownership logic? | Archive entries store nullable related ids (`relatedArtifactVersionId`, `relatedSourceProvenanceId`, `relatedToolCallId`). Read services enrich from existing artifact/source services and degrade per entry when related records are unavailable. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:60:| 8 | What pagination/indexing keeps reads bounded? | Convex indexes `archiveEntries` by `processId, sequence`, `archiveTurns` by `processId, turnIndex`, and derived views by `processId, updatedAt`. Fastify routes expose cursor pagination and default page limits. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:61:| 9 | What idempotency strategy prevents duplicate archive entries? | `appendArchiveEntry` checks `processId + finalizationKey`. A replay returns the existing entry or no-ops. Sequence assignment happens only on first append. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:70:archive the PRD requires for long-horizon context management.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:72:Epic 7 introduces canonical archive truth without tearing out the live surface.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:74:UI state. Separately, completed process objects are finalized into archive\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:78:The design is deliberately conservative around derived views. Turns and\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:80:archive entries. A derived turn or chunk candidate can be rebuilt from the\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:81:archive. If derivation fails, the archive remains readable. That property is\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:87:records. Archive entries may link to those records and show related context, but\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:96:| Processes | Core architecture | Finalization points and archive read access live under one project/process |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:97:| Archive | Core architecture | Primary Epic 7 domain; owns canonical entries and rebuildable projections |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:98:| Projects | Core architecture | Project/process access gates archive reads |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:99:| Artifacts | Core architecture | Provides related artifact-version context during archive reads |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:100:| Sources | Core architecture + Epic 6 | Provides related source provenance context during archive reads |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:101:| Client | Core architecture | Adds process-surface entry points for archive, turn, and structural-view reads |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:108:    FINAL[ArchiveFinalizationService]\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:110:    X[(Convex Archive Tables)]\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:111:    READ[ArchiveReadService]\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:113:    VIEWS[DerivedArchiveViewService]\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:114:    API[Fastify archive routes]\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:115:    UI[Client process/archive UI]\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:129:`ArchiveFinalizationService` when a process object is complete. The service\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:130:normalizes the finalized object into canonical archive entry shape and asks\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:133:The read path is broader. Fastify routes call `ArchiveReadService` for archive\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:134:entries, `TurnDerivationService` for turns, and `DerivedArchiveViewService` for\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:135:structural views. These services read durable archive data and enrich related\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:137:entry or view rather than hiding the archive.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:143:| Add new `archiveEntries` instead of replacing `processHistoryItems` | Current history is presentation-oriented and already used by live process surfaces | Epic 7 can preserve archive truth without destabilizing current UI |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:146:| Turns are cached projections | Long processes need bounded turn reads, but turns are derived | `archiveTurns` can be rebuilt from `archiveEntries` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:147:| Turn references must stay stable across rebuilds | Derived views cannot dangle when turn cache is refreshed | Turns get deterministic `turnId` values and derived views store stable turn ids plus turn-index ranges, not Convex row ids |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:148:| Derived views are structural only | Prevents scope creep into summarization | `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` contain boundaries/provenance, not generated summaries |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:157:├── archiveEntries.ts                         # NEW: append/read canonical archive entries\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:158:├── archiveTurns.ts                           # NEW: cached derived turn records\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:159:├── derivedArchiveViews.ts                    # NEW: structural derived-view records\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:160:└── schema.ts                                 # MODIFIED: archive tables and indexes\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:163:├── archive.ts                                # NEW: archive/turn/derived-view contracts and route builders\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:164:├── process-work-surface.ts                   # MODIFIED: optional archive entry points/actions in process surface contract\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:168:└── archive.ts                                # NEW: Fastify route schemas for archive APIs\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:171:└── archive.ts                                # NEW: authenticated archive/turn/derived-view routes\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:173:apps/platform/server/services/archive/\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:174:├── archive-finalization.service.ts           # NEW: finalized-object to archive-entry mapping\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:175:├── archive-read.service.ts                   # NEW: archive read/enrichment/degraded-state orchestration\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:177:├── deri