/test-plan.md:527:| `manifest entry is first in archive` | AC-5.2b invariant |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:530:| `Readable stream does not buffer entire archive in memory` | Streaming invariant (measure peak memory during large input) |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:541:| `cumulative byte counter rejects oversize archives` | Memory DoS defense |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/test-plan.md:754:16. Trigger an export on a fully-exportable package. Confirm the response includes a download link, download succeeds, and the `.mpkz` archive contains `_nav.md` + one entry per member.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:30:only, leaves archive and derived views to Epic 7, and defers MCP/external-source\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:84:time work is informed or code is updated. Archive entries in Epic 7 can link to\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:85:those provenance records without asking source attachments to become archive\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:99:| Archive | Core architecture | Downstream consumer only; Epic 6 provides source provenance that Epic 7 can reference |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:745:| Archive/turn/chunk views | Scope | Owned by Epic 7 | Epic 7 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/04-turn-derivation.md:5:Derive deterministic turn views from canonical archive entries, cache them as rebuildable projections, and preserve archive truth unchanged.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/04-turn-derivation.md:14:- **Key Constraint:** The archive must preserve