ve-view.test.ts` | canonical archive remains visible during derived-view failure |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/07-reopen-and-degraded-archive-state.md:134:| TC-7.3a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | archive read returns bounded page |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/07-reopen-and-degraded-archive-state.md:138:- `tests/service/client/archive-turns-section.test.ts`: bounded turn surface rendering preserves page state on reload\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/07-reopen-and-degraded-archive-state.md:142:- This story hardens durability and bounded-read behavior; it does not invent new archive data shapes.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/07-reopen-and-degraded-archive-state.md:163:- Archive and turn reads remain available after reload\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/07-reopen-and-degraded-archive-state.md:164:- Derived views remain readable after reload or rebuild from turns when possible\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/07-reopen-and-degraded-archive-state.md:165:- Derived-view failures do not block archive reads\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/07-reopen-and-degraded-archive-state.md:166:- Archive reads enforce default and maximum page limits and return `hasMore`/`nextCursor`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/tech-design-server.md:47:| Archive | Epic 2 adds visible process history only; the full canonical archive remains a later concern |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/tech-design-server.md:168:Do not implement the later archive/derived-view layer now. Epic 2 only needs\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/tech-design-server.md:170:current request projection. The full low-level archive taxonomy remains a later\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/tech-design-server.md:183:| `processHistoryItems` | NEW | Durable visible process history items for the process surface | User-facing history only, not full canonical archive |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:9:Epic 4 adds three new server concerns beneath the existing surface set: a dedicated review route family, a server-side markdown render pipeline, and a streaming export path that composes Convex File Storage content into a `.mpkz` archive. None of these are public products of their own — they are deeper implementation layers inside the existing authenticated application boundary.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:148:| `export.service.ts` | NEW | Two-phase export: POST returns `ExportPackageResponse` JSON with a signed download URL; GET at that URL (handled by the same `routes/review.ts` module) streams the `.mpkz` archive through `createPackageFromEntries` into the Fastify reply body | `PlatformStore`, `@liminal-build/markdown-package`, `export-url-signing` | AC-5 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:604:stay exportable because the archive packages pinned bytes, not the rendered\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:783:  // Phase 2: GET /exports/:exportId?token=... — verify token, stream the .mpkz archive\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1134:Export is a two-phase flow. Phase 1 is a POST that validates the export request, mints a signed download URL, and returns metadata. Phase 2 is a GET at the signed URL that streams the `.mpkz` archive bytes through `@liminal-build/markdown-package`'s `createPackageFromEntries` into the Fastify reply body. Splitting the two phases matches the spec's `ExportPackageResponse` contract (with `downloadUrl` + `expiresAt`), lets the client render a real download link before bytes flow, and gives expired-URL handling (AC-5.3b) a natural implementation.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1206:- **Member filenames.** Each member's archive filename is derived from its `displayName`. Markdown members use `.md`; unsupported-but-durable members still export their pinned bytes under a stable fallback filename rather than being filtered out. Collisions are resolved by appending `-{position}` to later duplicates.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1208:- **Download URL reuse semantics.** The signed URL is **reusable within the expiry window** — the same URL can be GET'd multiple times until `expiresAt`, each GET re-validates the token, re-checks access + exportability, and streams a fresh archive. No single-use enforcement. This lets users copy the download link, re-download after an interrupted transfer, or share within the expiry if they choose. After `expiresAt`, every GET returns 404 `REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND` regardless of how many prior downloads succeeded.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1210:- **Mid-stream failures** (e.g., Convex File Storage fetch fails for one member) tear down the HTTP response; the client sees a truncated download and re-exports. We do not attempt to recover a partial archive.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1233:| TC-5.1a (phase 2) | export download streams valid tar.gz | `tests/service/server/review-export-api.test.ts` | POST result's downloadUrl | GET returns 200 `application/gzip`; stream extracts to valid archive with expected members |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1236:| TC-5.2a | export matches reviewed versions | `tests/service/server/review-export-api.test.ts` | package pinned at V1; V2 also exists | extracted archive contains V1 bytes (not V2) |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1237:| TC-5.2b | export manifest | `tests/service/server/review-export-api.test.ts` | exported archive | extracted `_nav.md` contains package identity + member identities in package order |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1402:The returned `Readable` stream emits `.mpkz` (or `.mpk` if `compress: false`) bytes. Callers pipe it into a Fastify reply, a file system write stream, or any other consumer. The `manifest` is written as the first tar entry (`_nav.md`), followed by one entry per yielded `PackageEntry`. The `maxEntryBytes` and `maxTotalBytes` caps enforce bounded memory use per entry and bounded archive size overall; exceeding either terminates the stream with a `PackageError`.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:1442:1. **Decompression bomb protection**: every `createGunzip()` invocation passes `{ maxOutputLength: <cap> }`. The cap defaults to 256 MB per archive; `createPackageFromEntries` also enforces a per-entry `maxEntryBytes` cap (default 64 MB) inside its entry-processing loop.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:1:# Story 6: Archive Provenance Coherence\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:5:Enrich archive-entry reads with available artifact-version and source provenance while preserving derived-view traceability and owning per-entry lookup-failure degradation semantics.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:14:- **Key Constraint:** The archive must preserve finalized low-level entries as canonical truth. It must not store raw streaming deltas, interrupted partial objects, or only pre-summarized history as the durable record.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:18:Connect the Story 3 archive read surface to Epic 5 artifact-version provenance and Epic 6 source provenance without redefining artifact ownership or source attachment lifecycle.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:24:- Archive read enrichment for related artifact version context\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:25:- Archive read enrichment for related source provenance context\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:30:- Derived-view provenance traces through source turns to source archive entries\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:31:- Preserving Story 3 route/UI behavior while enriching the archive response contract\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:39:- Hiding archive entries because related records are unavailable\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:40:- Replacing Story 3 archive route, access, reload, or bounded-page behavior\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:47:- Existing archive read service and route\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:53:**AC-6.1:** Archive entries can show related artifact-version provenance when available.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:55:- **TC-6.1a: Artifact provenance visible from archive entry**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:56:  - Given: An archive entry relates to an artifact version\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:57:  - When: User reads the archive entry\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:60:**AC-6.2:** Archive entries can show related source provenance when available.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:62:- **TC-6.2a: Source provenance visible from archive entry**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:63:  - Given: An archive entry relates to a source that informed or received work\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:64:  - When: User reads the archive entry\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:67:**AC-6.3:** Missing related provenance does not hide archive truth.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:70:  - Given: An archive entry references source provenance that cannot be fully resolved\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:71:  - When: User reads the archive\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:72:  - Then: The archive entry remains visible with degraded source context\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:74:  - Given: An archive entry references artifact context that cannot be fully resolved\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:75:  - When: User reads the archive\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md:76:  - Then: The archive entry remains visible with degraded artifact context\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/06-archive-provenance-coherence.md: